# Sentinel v2 demo — a full 5-stage attack chain that v1 misses.
# Target: user `deploy`, a privileged service account.
# All IPs are RFC 5737 documentation ranges. Lab / sample data only.
#
# Stage 1 — LOW-AND-SLOW + DISTRIBUTED brute force (02:10-08:10, Nov 21):
#   18 failed logins for ONE user, from THREE IPs, ~3/hour.
#   v1 R001 needs 5 failures / 5 min from ONE IP — never fires.
#   v1 R004 needs 8 distinct users / 10 min — only 1 user, never fires.
# Stage 2 — Initial access 08:22, from an attacking IP.
# Stage 3 — Privilege escalation 08:30-08:40 (sudo failures, then root).
# Stage 4 — Lateral movement 09:05, deploy logs into db01 (never used before).
# Stage 5 — Data staging 09:20, tar + scp of /etc and /home on db01.
# Normal noise (alice/bob on web01, 08:00-09:00) is interleaved so the
# chain must be linked by user/IP/host, not by taking every event.
